      "calculationScope": "EXACT_MANUAL_CALCULATION",
      "manualArithmetic": "The source assigns symbolic relations, not compulsory numerical data. Current is signed net charge divided by time (or its instantaneous rate); negative electron charge times opposite signed carrier flux yields the conventional direction. Combining J=E/rho, E=V/length and I=JA gives R=rho*length/area. Differentiate V=RI versus I=V/R to distinguish slopeR from1/R. Constructed manual probes:6C/3s=2A, -6C/3s=-2A,6V/3ohm=2A, lengthfactor2 doublesR and radiusfactor2 givesonequarterR. The polynomial heating probe has slope1+3I² rather than a constant: it is outside the fixed-temperature ohmic model, not a claim that the lesson requires this derivative.",
      "manualFeasibility": "PASS_AI_EXACT",
      "physicalAssumptions": "Current relative to chosen section direction; average ratio for finite interval, constant-current shortcut only when constant. Ohmic material at fixed assigned temperature. Uniform homogeneous wire, positive finite length/cross-section/resistivity. DeltaV in resistor law is explicitly a passive voltage drop, not unqualified VB-VA. Ideal generator fixes voltage, not current.",
      "pedagogicalReview": "Separates reference direction from electron motion; defines ideal generator and axis-dependent slope before formula manipulation; fixes temperature and geometry for resistivity law. No numerical work is waived merely because the record has no answer field.",
