      "calculationScope": "EXACT_MANUAL_CALCULATION",
      "manualArithmetic": "Source derivations: common seriesI givesV=I(R1+R2); common parallelV givesI=V(1/R1+1/R2). ThusReq=R1R2/(R1+R2), with positive gapsRi-Req. SubstituteOhm intoVI to obtainI²R andV²/R, retaining passive signs. ConstantP givesE=P*duration; varyingP requires integral. Constructed manual probes:2+3=5ohm, inverse(1/2+1/3)=6/5ohm,6V*2A=12W and12W*3s=36J. ForP(t)=2t over0..3s the integral is9J, not endpointP timesduration18J. Across separate trials at fixed sourceV a series memberP1=V²R1/(R1+R2)² is nonmonotonic; the source compares commonI within a series circuit and does not assert unchangedI when loadchanges.",
      "manualFeasibility": "PASS_AI_EXACT",
      "physicalAssumptions": "Ideal wires define equipotential nodes, lumped quasi-static/steady resistive circuit without accumulating nodal charge. Positive finite linear resistances. Series requires an unbranched shared node; parallel requires same two nodes. VI is absorbed power under passive convention; E=P*duration only for constantP. CommonI/commonV comparisons concern components under the stated constraint.",
      "pedagogicalReview": "Defines topology through node connections rather than drawn proximity; derives equivalents; compares power only after identifying held-current or held-voltage constraint. Constant-power energy qualifier is explicit.",
